Original commit body from 4d8c7d2:

When a module is imported via "from app import crud" and then used as
"crud.create_user()", the call was incorrectly resolved as unresolved.

Root cause: `from X import Y` is always stored in symbol_imports, but
when Y is a submodule (not a symbol defined in X), the call resolution
failed to find it.

Fix: Added Case 2e in _process_call() to try submodule lookup when the
imported name isn't found as a class symbol. If we have "from app import
crud" and call "crud.create_user()", we now try looking up (app.crud,
create_user) which correctly resolves to the function.

This fixes the P1 issue from bakeoff 12.15 where FastAPI routes calling
crud.create_user() emitted unresolved edges instead of proper call edges.
